# WITHOUT THIS FILE, `gcloud run deploy --source .` DERIVES ITS UPLOAD LIST FROM .gitignore
# -- and .gitignore excludes artifacts/, which is the index. The build would then fail on
# `COPY artifacts/d1/s7`, pointing at a Dockerfile line that is perfectly correct. This file
# exists to say the opposite of .gitignore about exactly one directory.
.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
# keys are set with `gcloud run deploy --set-env-vars` / Secret Manager, never uploaded
.env
# gigabytes of source shards; the frozen corpus in data/ is what the index was built from
data/raw/
data/shards/
data/audio/
.backup-*/
*.pdf
# only the winning strategy ships. The other seven indexes are 420 MB of evidence for
# reports/chunking.md, and the container serves exactly one of them -- the one
# reports/chunking.json names.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/d1
artifacts/d1/*
!artifacts/d1/s7
deploy/
DEPLOY.md
OBJECTIVE.md
